verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED: install v4.38.386.14, load crafted extension/page into sidebar web-panel and devtools-in-sidebar; test sandbox escape / cross-origin XHR-fetch / CSP bypass; repro-first on latest; zero server interaction
impact: cross-origin data theft or script execution in browser UI; High–Critical (escalation to renderer)
testability: AUTH_HELPED

STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE
- [PARKED] Scrapbook shared-category invite-link authorization: v4.38.386.12 changelog marks it "별도 배포 예정" (coming soon) → feature not reproducible on LATEST → violates latest-version requirement until it ships
- [PARKED] Bundled-libs version drift (conf 35 < 40): no manifest, generic diff-only path, repeated across runs
- [MODERATED] Sync KDF hypothesis: desktop likely inherits Chromium's audited scrypt (Chromium is forked) → generic KDF weakness is low-prob; live sub-vector reframed to Android's late/custom 2025-04 implementation (conf 58→55)
- [FINAL] 1. Sync passphrase KDF / client key-storage — Android impl (AUTH, 55) 2. Multiplay session scoping / URL-only boundary (AUTH, 50) 3. Sidebar + DevTools-in-sidebar boundary (OTHER, 50)

STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION
- [NEXT] HUMAN: authorized two-account test on Whale v4.38.386.14 Multiplay — host opens a login-gated page and a page with a token-bearing query string; joiner joins via copied invite link; record file-local whether host's excluded login URLs or token params reach the joiner (tab list/URL sync/notifications) and whether the invite link still works after host leaves (auto-delete); zero requests to naver sync infra. This is the only top lead whose falsifiable evidence exists and does NOT depend on the blocked binary acquisition (apkpure/APKMirror 403, installer.whale.naver.com 404, repo docs-only).

STEP 6 — LEARNING
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED AUTH @ Multiplay: vendor documents URL-only sharing + own-account rendering + login-page auto-exclusion → cross-account boundary is explicit, documented, and falsifiable on latest
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED AUTH @ sync client: passphrase client-side-only model re-confirmed in primary sources ("neither sent to NAVER nor saved on its server"; reset deletes server data + logs out all devices) → KDF analysis is a live class
- [LEARN] REJECTED OTHER @ Scrapbook invite-link: category invite-by-link marked "coming soon / 별도 배포 예정" in v4.38.386.12 changelog → not reproducible on latest → not reportable
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ sidebar: v4.38.386.12 changelog confirms Chrome Side Panel spec + DevTools-in-sidebar shipped on the recurring CVE surface

STEP 7 — RISK SCORE
- [RISK] sync: 58 — Multiplay GA adds real-time URL/tab sync with a documented but unverifiable cross-account boundary; Scrapbook short-URL links (30-day TTL) expand the shared-data plane; passphrase client-side KDF confirmed but mobile impl custom/late (2025-04); binary unavailable blocks static verification
- [RISK] browser: 78 — sidebar+DevTools-in-sidebar fresh code on a 6-CVE recurring surface; download-warning bypass just patched (active hardening); CVE-2026-11645 inherited (KEV) but not reportable; latest-version repro is the main gate
- [RISK] libs: 30 — no Whale-only bundled-lib manifest; installer DLL family recurring but pre-3.1.0.0 (local, old); no inventory possible without the binary
