## STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] Acquired official v4.38.386.14 Linux client binary (naver-whale-stable_amd64.deb, 164,163,916 bytes, installer-whale.pstatic.net, last-modified 2026-06-25) — first full client binary in hand; prior KB asserted "no browser binary source for static analysis," now refuted (installer CDN, not the doc-only GitHub repo)
- [NEW] Static strings confirm Whale sync is a **custom transport**, not Google sync: `https://api.whale.naver.com/whalesync` + `/whalesync/reset`; auth via NID OAuth on apis.naver.com (`/oauth2/v1/nid/login`, `/oauth2/v1/nid/refresh`, `/oauth2/v1/nid/epoch/v1`); headers `X-Whale-Access-Token: %s`, `X-Whale-SigninType`, `X-Whale-Version`, `X-Whale-Platform`; cookies `NEO_SES`/`NID_SES`/`NID_AUT`, `__Host-session_id`/`__Host-session_csrf`
- [NEW] Synced data types (whalesync request field list): apps, autofill, **bookmarks, cookies, extensions, passwords, preferences**, productComparison, readingList, savedTabGroups, tabs, themes, typedUrls — **passwords + cookies + tabs sync over the custom endpoint**
- [NEW] Whale-only encryption prefs not present in upstream Chromium: `sync.encryption_bootstrap_token_per_account`, `sync.encryption_bootstrap_token_per_account_migration_done`, `sync.whale_need_encryption_key_forced_time`, `sync.passphrase_prompt_muted_product_version` (paired with `nigori-key`, `sync_pb.EncryptionKeys`, `syncDataEncryptedText`)
- [NEW] Bundled real-time push extension `whale_sync_push` (`service_worker.js` + `socket.io.slim.js`) in resources.pak — Whale-only socket.io channel feeding the sync engine
- [NEW] Local key storage on Linux = OSCrypt (KWallet/Libsecret) via `.ReencryptedWithAsyncOSCrypt` / `OSCrypt using KWallet/Libsecret` backends
- [CHANGED] Prior "REJECTED browser source" applies only to GitHub repo; client binary is obtainable from the official CDN → static analysis of sync engine now feasible (state target=sync, phase=POC)
- NO_DELTA: NVD still 21 CVEs / 0 in 2026; repo last push 2019-09-23; wiki has no sync docs (5 pages, none sync)

